  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowerment of vulnerable youth in Lebanon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the project is to continue the established club in Bourj Hammoud, Beirut, and proceed to offer a safe space for the 60 youths aged 13 to 18, primarily from Syria and Lebanon. In the club the youths gather to socialise and learn new skills in the classes e.g. music, acting and media, as well as excursions and workshops focusing on volunteerism, gender equality, youth influence and legal counselling. By engaging in these activities, the youths will enhance their personal, professional, and societal capacities, contributing to positive change in their local community. The project seeks to empower youths, foster skills, and build networks for lasting impact.</narrative>
  </description>
